[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444128830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4444128830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4444128830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCOQGPg","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T18:32:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T18:42:26Z","body":"It's a little hard to follow the code in godot-cpp, but I suspect what's happening is that we're immediately destructing the original array, and then assigning a new one. If so, this isn't ideal.\n\nSince `Array` has its own internal reference mechanism, I think it would be better for the original to made into a reference to the new array, but I don't think we have a function in the GDExtension interface that would allow us to do that. But if we added one, then bindings could start adopting that without breaking compatibility.\n\nI think it's the same situation with `Dictionary`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444128830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444533868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4444533868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4444533868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCOo0bA","user":{"login":"Splizard","id":2015791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTU3OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2015791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard","html_url":"https://github.com/Splizard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T19:26:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T19:26:08Z","body":"Is this the same for virtual calls and calls into the engine too? This is honestly unexpected behavior (and a bit of a footgun). Are there any callees known to be using the pre-initialized result? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444533868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444645905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4444645905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4444645905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCOvqEQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T19:43:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T19:43:23Z","body":"> Is this the same for virtual calls and calls into the engine too?\n\nI think so (again, some of this code is very hard to follow)\n\n> Are there any callees known to be using the pre-initialized result?\n\nWe'd have to check all existing GDExtension bindings and see what they do. Any of them certainly could be using the pre-initialized Array/Dictionary.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4444645905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445314039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4445314039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4445314039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCPYb9w","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T21:23:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T21:23:09Z","body":"So far I've only found Dictionary and Array to be passing anything other than a nil or zero init.\nOthers which allocate into medium memory bucket like AABB pass the pointer to the mem bucket, so there's no issue with those. They would be cleaned up once the stack exits.\n\nCalling into the engine seems fine. Those are all copies from data into the pointer you passed in. So don't pass an array or dictionary that's already initialized. I think that would be a mem leak if you do. But I haven't looked at this section in great detail.\nThose go through these helpers: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/aaaf76403e88a3316073f8506672d7e88f167df8/core/variant/binder_common.h#L89","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4445314039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4450467125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4450467125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4450467125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCUS9NQ","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T12:00:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T12:00:42Z","body":"Really we just need the = overload or _ref in order to unref the old Array and Dictionary.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9a33066a27d70c6d4f74cae44c1ce023d8082a59/core/variant/array.cpp#L56\n\nWhat we are looking for was deprecated array_ref.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9a33066a27d70c6d4f74cae44c1ce023d8082a59/core/extension/gdextension_interface.cpp#L1298\n\n> Deprecated in Godot 4.5. Removed from interface. Use copy constructor instead.\n\nWhich one is the copy constructor?\nThe closest constructor I can see sets _p to nullptr before calling _ref.. which means no unref.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9a33066a27d70c6d4f74cae44c1ce023d8082a59/core/variant/array.cpp#L952\n\nI haven't looked into dictionary beyond the fact that there was no ref function for dictionary in the GDE header.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4450467125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451061363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451061363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451061363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCU3Ocw","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T13:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T13:27:16Z","body":"> What we are looking for was deprecated array_ref.\n\nAh, it looks like it was deprecated in PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/82497\n\nProbably part of the reason we couldn't justify its existence at the time, was that godot-cpp didn't use it. Based on @Bromeon's approval there, I'm assuming Rust didn't use it either.\n\nSo, we could undeprecate that function (or make a new `2` version) and then add a `dictionary_ref` to go along with it as well\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451061363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451203117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451203117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451203117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCU_4LQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T13:42:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T13:42:25Z","body":"I made a quick draft PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119461) for what this could look like, but I haven't had a chance to test it yet","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451203117/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451288646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451288646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451288646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCVFGRg","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T13:52:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T13:52:57Z","body":"I watched the video but I'm still not quite sure why we'd need to bring the deprecated `_ref()` methods back.\nWhat does this enable that is currently not possible? Is it purely an optimization? \n@Ferinzz could you update the initial PR description to clearly outline the motivation of this change?\n\nAlso, would such methods not be needed also for `Packed*Array` or even `Variant`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451288646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451362147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451362147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451362147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCVJlYw","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T14:02:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T14:02:04Z","body":"> What does this enable that is currently not possible? Is it purely an optimization?\n\nIt's an optimization, potentially.\n\nWhen Godot does a ptrcall to a function defined in GDExtension, and that function returns an Array or Dictionary, it will initialize a new Array or Dictionary into the return value. However, in some language bindings (including godot-cpp), it just immediately destructs that Array or Dictionary and then makes a new one in its place.\n\nThis would allow making the original Array or Dictionary a reference to the new Array or Dictionary instead\n\nI'm not sure this optimization actually matters, though. :-) We're still initializing a `ArrayPrivate` or `DictionaryPrivate` when the original Array or Dictionary is created, and then deleting it when referencing the new Array or Dictionary. So, it really just limits us to deleting 1 thing right away, rather than 2. So, it might not be worth doing?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451362147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451397103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451397103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451397103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCVLt7w","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T14:06:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T14:14:22Z","body":"Not needed for packed*array because for whatever reason the default init initializes them with 0 reference and they subsequently destroys themselves. :D (an issue for another day)\ncallable, string, stringname were also concerns but from testing they did not have this issue.\n\nI used the array_ref and it worked for this scenario. I can do some testing of the branch tomorrow if others haven't already.\n\nWhat other option is there apart from a ffi call to destroy and then an ffi call to create1? What is the copy constructor which was mentioned in the deprecation comment? I'll be happy to test that.\n\nSince there is a concern that someone somewhere might be relying on this empty array we can't do the real optimization which would be to simply not initialize the array/dictionary.  Clear data, set the type, and pass the pointer to the _mem data section. Otherwise we need to report a breaking change warning?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451397103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451624857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4451624857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4451624857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCVZnmQ","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T14:32:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T14:32:00Z","body":"\n> @Ferinzz could you update the initial PR description to clearly outline the motivation of this change?\n\nCould you please do this? Your description describes what's happening, but not why this is not enough. Also in light of existing GDExtension working fine despite this. (Basically add dsnopek's explanation + some motivation).\n\nIt would also be nice if you could list potential downsides -- when is `array_ref` safe to use; is there a chance to mess up lifetimes or run into UB if used incorrectly?\n\nSorry for being pedantic here, but this seems like a very low-level operation that may introduce more bugs when used incorrectly, and for a performance improvement it's not clear in which order of magnitude we're talking 🙂 \n\n---\n\nAlso, if it's an optimization, should this issue not be labeled \"performance\" rather than \"bug\"?\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451624857/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4452207201","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4452207201","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4452207201,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCV9KYQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T15:40:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T15:40:15Z","body":"> Since there is a concern that someone somewhere might be relying on this empty array we can't do the real optimization which would be to simply not initialize the array/dictionary. Clear data, set the type, and pass the pointer to the _mem data section. Otherwise we need to report a breaking change warning?\n\nWe could theoretically \"do the real optimization\", which would be changing the ptrcall convention to say the pointer to the return value contains uninitialized memory (rather than currently it contains a pointer to memory initialized to the default value), and requiring the bindings to always initialize that memory.\n\nIn order to maintain compatibility, we'd need to make new GDExtension interface functions (ie incrementing the suffix `2` -> `3`, etc) in every place that we register a callback that is called with the ptrcall convention, and then have Godot use either the old or new ptrcall convention depending on which function was used to register them.\n\nSo, it's possible to do, but would require a bunch more work, which would need to be done a whole lot more delicately.\n\nPerhaps we should be making some benchmarks before going too much further. It would be nice to have some numbers for:\n\n- Things as the are now\n- Switching to using `array_ref` and `dictionary_ref` for assigning the array\n- Changing the ptrcall convention to not initialize the memory on the Godot side","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4452207201/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4453154880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4453154880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4453154880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCW3AQA","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T17:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T17:35:31Z","body":"> In order to maintain compatibility, we'd need to make new GDExtension interface functions (ie incrementing the suffix `2` -> `3`, etc) in every place that we register a callback that is called with the ptrcall convention, and then have Godot use either the old or new ptrcall convention depending on which function was used to register them.\n\nI imagine adding an additional branch into the call would reduce any impact performance improvements from this could gain. I will try and do some testing over the weekend just to see what it looks like. :)\nKeeping it as-is would align with how it is handling types such as AABB; Projection; Transform2D/3D which is an initialized container for it. If we go with that logic, it is an even stronger reason to include something such as array_ref which re-uses the array class container.\n\n@Bromeon let me know if the initial issue description is more or less clear or if something feels missing.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4453154880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4454979043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4454979043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4454979043,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCYmV4w","user":{"login":"Splizard","id":2015791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTU3OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2015791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard","html_url":"https://github.com/Splizard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splizard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T21:44:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T21:46:22Z","body":"It's just so weird having this distinction between 'initialized' results and 'uninitialized' as part of the gdextension calling convention. What value does this provide? Where is this useful? Why should the caller ever initialize an array/dictionary return value in this way? \n\nSure there's a comment at the top of the header that says this distinction is important but the case that @Ferinzz discovered is an incredibly subtle consequence of this 'convention' that more often than not ends in an inadvertent memory leak.\n\nI don't agree this is a 'performance' issue, it's a footgun at the bare minimum and if you don't want to change anything here; something we need to raise awareness on. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4454979043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4458620611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4458620611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4458620611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCcEmww","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T09:27:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T09:27:50Z","body":"> It's just so weird having this distinction between 'initialized' results and 'uninitialized' as part of the gdextension calling convention. What value does this provide? Where is this useful? Why should the caller ever initialize an array/dictionary return value in this way?\n\nVariants. Variant's memory layout is complicated and as a result it makes certain types complicated to handle. Packed arrays are weird.\nAs a result Godot can't pass us a pointer to the Variant.data field and say \"have at it\" for each and every case.\n\nIf we are to have a non-initialized version we would need Godot to manage insertion of the data into the Variant. (at least for this specific path) which may have refCounting implications and new rules to follow.\n\nI haven't looked into virtuals yet.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4458620611/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4470717394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119440#issuecomment-4470717394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119440","id":4470717394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCnm70g","user":{"login":"Ferinzz","id":44227010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjI3MDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44227010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz","html_url":"https://github.com/Ferinzz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ferinzz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-17T12:49:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T12:49:44Z","body":"Using the following regex I looked for virtuals which might have type initialization. The search was done in the extension_api.json file\n```regex\n\t\t\t\t\t\"is_virtual\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"hash\": .*,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"return_value\": \\{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"Dic\n```\n24 virtuals with Dictionary as return\n31 with typedarray as return\n4 with Array as return\n6 return pointers of some kind (2 void* 4 const Glyph*)\n\nI haven't gotten to implementing any of these virtuals yet. Cannot test in a real implementation. @Splizard have you been able to check any of these virtuals with dictionary/array returns?\n\nWould this line cause RAII initialization?\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/321b8c944fa32ee94eef44a56925105d7091be03/core/object/script_language_extension.h#L306\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/321b8c944fa32ee94eef44a56925105d7091be03/core/object/script_language_extension.h#L394\n\nNotifications don't pass data, so those shouldn't need to be verified.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4470717394/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]